# {{.project_name}}

Secure Electron + React desktop app generated by smokeforge.

## Stack

- Electron `45.3.3`, React `19.3.0`, TypeScript `5.9.3`
- electron-vite `6.0.0`, Vite `7.3.8`, electron-builder `26.18.0`
- React Router 8, Tailwind CSS 4, shadcn/ui, lucide-react, sonner
- cmdk, react-resizable-panels, Recharts, TanStack Table/Virtual
- Zod, React Hook Form, i18next, date-fns, dnd-kit, motion
- Drizzle ORM + drizzle-kit on better-sqlite3
- electron-log, electron-updater, electron-window-state
- Optional TanStack Query, Zustand, and Playwright Electron
- Package manager: `{{.package_manager}}` (pnpm, npm, or bun)

## Code layout

```text
src/
  main/                 trusted Node/Electron process
    index.ts            entry point
    bootstrap.ts        composition root and app lifecycle
    app/                protocol, native menu, app wiring
    windows/            main and detached BrowserWindow factories
    security/           CSP, permissions, navigation guards
    ipc/                one validated IPC wrapper and registration
    features/           system, settings, activity, updates, windows
    infra/              config, paths, electron-log, typed JSON settings
    storage/            Drizzle schema, repositories, and migrations
    workers/            utilityProcess job entry points
  preload/              narrow contextBridge API
  renderer/             sandboxed React app
    src/app/            hash router, providers, route error boundary
    src/components/     shell layout and shadcn/ui primitives
    src/features/       dashboard, library, activity, settings, account, about
    src/lib/            desktop API client, i18n, query helpers, stores
  shared/               code imported by trusted and sandboxed sides
    ipc/                channel names and Zod schemas
    types/              Result and desktop API contracts
drizzle/                committed SQL migrations and drizzle metadata
resources/              icons, entitlements, installer assets
tests/
  unit/                 pure unit tests
  ipc/                  IPC boundary tests
  e2e/                  Playwright Electron tests
docs/                   architecture, design, security, storage, updates, packaging
```

## Commands

```bash
make install
make dev           # hot reload: renderer HMR, preload reload, main restart
make dev-inspect   # dev + V8 inspector on the main process (port 5858)
make test
make typecheck
make build
make package

# SQLite schema change
pnpm db:generate
```

The first install creates the lockfile; commit it afterward.

See [docs/DEVELOPMENT.md](docs/DEVELOPMENT.md) for what reloads on save, the
development Content-Security-Policy, and main-process debugging.

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    Renderer[Sandboxed renderer] -->|typed functions| Preload[preload contextBridge]
    Preload -->|validated IPC| Main[main process]
    Main --> Security[security policy]
    Main --> Features[feature services]
    Features --> API[API client / filesystem / safeStorage]
    Main --> Result[Result<T>]
    Result --> Preload
    Preload --> Renderer
```

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Dev[Development] --> Vite[electron-vite dev server]
    Prod[Production] --> Protocol[app://bundle protocol]
    Vite --> Window[BrowserWindow]
    Protocol --> Window
    Window --> Preload
```

## Local data

- Preferences use `src/main/infra/settings.ts`: a versioned JSON store with
  validation, atomic writes, and corrupt-file quarantine.
- Durable app data uses SQLite through Drizzle in `src/main/storage/`. Keep it
  in the main process and expose it through validated IPC. Generate migrations
  with `make`/`pnpm db:generate`, never with `push` against user data.
- Tokens and secrets belong in `safeStorage`, never JSON or SQLite.
- Settings > Data exports/imports Library JSON and creates SQLite backups.
- Settings > Advanced can enable a daily WAL checkpoint (off by default).
- Offline outbox/sync and watched folders are separate features; SQLite is not a
  second server database, and folder watching is intentionally not enabled.

## Security boundary

The renderer has no Node.js access. It calls only `window.desktopApi`.
The preload script exposes a narrow typed API. The main process validates every
IPC payload with Zod, checks the sender origin, and returns a stable
`{ ok, data } | { ok: false, error }` result.

Never disable `contextIsolation`, `sandbox`, or `webSecurity`. Never enable
`nodeIntegration`. Never expose raw `ipcRenderer`, filesystem, shell, or process
objects to the renderer. Tokens and secrets belong in the main process, not the
renderer.

Read `CONTEXT.md` before changing code, `DESIGN.md` before visual work, and
`docs/LIBRARIES.md` before adding a dependency, `docs/UI.md` before changing the shell, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`
before moving modules, `docs/STORAGE.md` before changing local data, and
`docs/SECURITY.md` before touching the IPC or session boundary.

Use the project-scoped `react-router`, `frontend-ui-engineering`, and `drizzle`
skills before changing routing, components, or local data. Refresh the component
skill with:

```bash
npx skills add https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills --skill frontend-ui-engineering
```

Refresh the Drizzle skill with:

```bash
npx skills add https://github.com/lobehub/lobehub --skill drizzle
``` Add shadcn primitives with
`pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <component> --yes` (or the npm/bun equivalent).

